  <p class="page-kicker">Head to head</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">ALFA AC1900 USB Wi-Fi Adapter vs Built-in Laptop Wi-Fi</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">Built-in Wi-Fi cards in laptops use tiny internal antennas tucked around the screen bezel. In a good-signal room they work fine. In a weak-signal room they struggle. An external USB adapter with big physical antennas can pull useful signal where the built-in card sees nothing. Here is when to spend the $50.</p>

